1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:03,420
God, you're beautiful.

2
00:00:03,462 --> 00:00:06,423
Why are we fighting this?

3
00:00:06,465 --> 00:00:09,468
You know you want it
to happen as much as I do.

4
00:00:10,928 --> 00:00:12,304
I want you.

5
00:00:12,346 --> 00:00:14,181
I need you.

6
00:00:17,476 --> 00:00:19,353
Let me make love to you.

7
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:21,480
Now, I don't want
to stand in the way

8
00:00:21,522 --> 00:00:22,898
of true love or anything,

9
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:25,567
but I think a cantaloupe
might hurt less.

10
00:00:25,609 --> 00:00:27,528
No, I'm, uh...

11
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:29,321
I'm rehearsing my lines.

12
00:00:29,363 --> 00:00:32,073
They're giving me a big romantic
story on Days of Our Lives.

13
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:33,951
It's the first time
my character's gotten one.

14
00:00:33,993 --> 00:00:34,994
I'm so nervous, you know?

15
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:36,161
I really want it to be good.

16
00:00:36,203 --> 00:00:37,329
Wow.

17
00:00:37,371 --> 00:00:38,956
I haven't seen you
this worked up

18
00:00:38,998 --> 00:00:40,749
since you did
that dog food commercial

19
00:00:40,791 --> 00:00:43,585
and you thought you were going
to be with a real talking dog.

20
00:00:45,379 --> 00:00:47,756
Yeah, that was a disappointment.

21
00:00:47,798 --> 00:00:48,841
Ooh, hey.

22
00:00:48,883 --> 00:00:50,425
You want to come down to the set

23
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:51,886
and tell me if I'm
doing okay?

24
00:00:51,927 --> 00:00:53,679
Are you serious?
Yeah, yeah.

25
00:00:53,721 --> 00:00:55,681
You just have to promise
not to get yourself

26
00:00:55,723 --> 00:00:56,765
thrown out again.

27
00:00:56,807 --> 00:00:58,684
That was an honest mistake.

28
00:00:58,726 --> 00:00:59,935
Right.

29
00:00:59,977 --> 00:01:01,770
"Oh, my God.
Is this the men's room?

30
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:03,397
"I feel so foolish.

31
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:06,901
Have you always known
you wanted to be an actor?"

32
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:11,112
Yeah, that was an awesome day.

33
00:01:17,995 --> 00:01:22,708
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

34
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:24,960
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

35
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:28,047
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

36
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:32,551
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

37
00:01:32,593 --> 00:01:35,054
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

38
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:37,472
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

39
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:41,226
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

40
00:01:41,268 --> 00:01:47,274
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

41
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,070
Hey.

42
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:52,071
Hey.

43
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:53,530
Hi.

44
00:01:53,572 --> 00:01:55,115
So, do you guys want
to come and eat dinner

45
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:56,992
at the restaurant sometime
in the next few weeks?

46
00:01:57,034 --> 00:01:58,493
Sure, yeah.
Oh, we'd love to.

47
00:01:58,535 --> 00:01:59,912
Well, you can't.

48
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:03,248
We're booked solid
for the next month.

49
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:04,833
Well, I can't
give you a massage

50
00:02:04,875 --> 00:02:07,086
because my license
has been revoked again.

51
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:09,838
Phoebe, what happened?

52
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,339
Well, it was an accident.

53
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:12,925
You know, it's a lot of oil

54
00:02:12,967 --> 00:02:15,803
and sometimes
the hand just slips.

55
00:02:17,429 --> 00:02:19,347
Have I got a surprise for you.

56
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:20,599
Pack your bags.

57
00:02:20,641 --> 00:02:22,267
Oh, no.

58
00:02:22,309 --> 00:02:25,020
You guys aren't supposed
to get divorced for seven years.

59
00:02:26,354 --> 00:02:27,898
What? No.

60
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:29,858
I'm taking Monica
to a romantic inn in Vermont.

61
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,192
Oh, good.

62
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:33,320
Okay.
Good for you.

63
00:02:33,361 --> 00:02:35,572
Trying to recapture the magic.
Good.

64
00:02:35,614 --> 00:02:36,782
So, what
do you say?

65
00:02:36,824 --> 00:02:38,283
Can you get
out of work?

66
00:02:38,325 --> 00:02:39,326
Oh, honey, I can't.

67
00:02:39,367 --> 00:02:40,744
I was just telling these guys

68
00:02:40,786 --> 00:02:41,996
that things are crazy
at the restaurant.

69
00:02:42,037 --> 00:02:43,204
You're really that busy?

70
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:45,582
Yeah. I'm sorry, I really am.

71
00:02:45,624 --> 00:02:46,875
Well,
that's okay.

72
00:02:46,917 --> 00:02:49,586
I'll just, uh,
try and reschedule.

73
00:02:50,754 --> 00:02:52,631
Hi, this is Chandler Bing.

74
00:02:52,673 --> 00:02:56,175
I made a reservation there
and I need to change it.

75
00:02:56,217 --> 00:02:58,679
Well, what do you mean
it's nonrefundable?

76
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:01,015
Well, can I just come
some other time?

77
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:03,684
Well, can't you
make an exception?

78
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:06,687
Tell them I'm a chef
at a big New York restaurant.

79
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:08,480
And tell them that in two weeks,

80
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:11,358
I will once again
be a masseuse in good standing.

81
00:03:13,110 --> 00:03:14,528
Look, this is ridiculous.

82
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:16,488
I'm not paying
for that room, okay?

83
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,073
Well thank you very much.

84
00:03:19,491 --> 00:03:21,618
Yeah, I'm going to Vermont.

85
00:03:22,703 --> 00:03:23,912
Oh, don't worry about it.

86
00:03:23,954 --> 00:03:25,204
Just use your
travel insurance.

87
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:26,665
I don't have travel insurance.

88
00:03:26,707 --> 00:03:28,167
Well, this
is what happens

89
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:30,002
when people
live on the edge.

90
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:32,754
Why don't you take Ross?

91
00:03:32,796 --> 00:03:35,632
Don't you think that'll
be a little weird?

92
00:03:35,674 --> 00:03:38,093
I mean, two guys
in a romantic inn?

93
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:40,679
No, not if the room
has two beds.

94
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:42,014
I guess.

95
00:03:42,056 --> 00:03:43,222
Still seems a little...

96
00:03:43,264 --> 00:03:46,267
Moonlight boat ride!

97
00:03:50,814 --> 00:03:52,232
Hey, Joey, is this the bed

98
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:54,026
where Olivia
lost her virginity?

99
00:03:54,068 --> 00:03:56,653
I don't know, but one
of the extras sure did.

100
00:03:56,695 --> 00:03:58,072
Hey, listen, Rach.

101
00:03:58,113 --> 00:04:00,532
Thanks again for coming
down to watch my scenes.

102
00:04:00,574 --> 00:04:02,201
Oh, please, honey.

103
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:03,952
Just the fact that you
want me here to support you...

104
00:04:03,994 --> 00:04:05,537
Oh, my God.

105
00:04:05,579 --> 00:04:07,748
Is that Christian Saunders?

106
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:09,249
He is so gorgeous.

107
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:11,585
Also, so gay.

108
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:13,170
Well...

109
00:04:13,212 --> 00:04:16,215
in my head, he's done some
pretty not-gay stuff.

110
00:04:16,255 --> 00:04:17,883
Well, at the Christmas party,

111
00:04:17,925 --> 00:04:20,301
him and Santa did some
definitely-gay stuff.

112
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:21,469
MAN:
Joey.

113
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:22,971
Joey, we're ready for you.

114
00:04:23,013 --> 00:04:24,056
Okay.

115
00:04:24,098 --> 00:04:25,473
All right,
wish me luck.

116
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:26,683
Okay.

117
00:04:26,725 --> 00:04:27,935
Well, not that you
need it, but good...

118
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:29,269
God! Is that
Chase Lassiter?

119
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,312
Oh, now he's straight,
right?

120
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:32,940
Rach, I got to say,

121
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:34,900
if you weren't here wondering
if these guys were gay,

122
00:04:34,942 --> 00:04:36,401
I don't know if I could do this.

123
00:04:36,443 --> 00:04:38,237
I'm sorry, you're right.

124
00:04:38,277 --> 00:04:39,404
I'm sorry. Good luck.

125
00:04:39,446 --> 00:04:40,781
Thanks.

126
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:45,368
And... action!

127
00:04:46,954 --> 00:04:48,413
Drake, what are
you doing here?

128
00:04:48,455 --> 00:04:49,414
Stopping you

129
00:04:49,456 --> 00:04:50,958
from marrying the wrong man

130
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:53,001
and making the biggest
mistake of your life.

131
00:04:53,043 --> 00:04:54,253
Get out.

132
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:55,336
You don't love him.

133
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,131
What do you know about love?

134
00:04:57,172 --> 00:05:00,092
I know what I felt that night
when we kissed under the bridge.

135
00:05:00,134 --> 00:05:02,219
That kiss
never happened.

136
00:05:02,261 --> 00:05:03,929
Well what about
this one?

137
00:05:03,971 --> 00:05:04,972
( gasps )

138
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:07,682
Now I told you
to get out.

139
00:05:07,724 --> 00:05:10,936
Fine,
I'll go.

140
00:05:10,978 --> 00:05:13,396
But let me ask you
one question.

141
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:14,606
You look real familiar.

142
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:15,857
Have we...
Shh!

143
00:05:15,899 --> 00:05:18,110
He's asking her a question.

144
00:05:18,152 --> 00:05:20,821
Can you really live
the rest of your life

145
00:05:20,862 --> 00:05:23,031
never knowing what
we could have been?

146
00:05:23,073 --> 00:05:24,449
I don't have a choice.

147
00:05:24,491 --> 00:05:25,492
Yes, you do.

148
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:27,786
Yes, you do.

149
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:30,371
I'm the one who doesn't
have a choice because I...

150
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:32,833
because I can't
stop loving you.

151
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:35,585
Don't say that.

152
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:38,255
Tell me to stop.

153
00:05:38,297 --> 00:05:42,050
Just... tell me to stop.

154
00:05:44,303 --> 00:05:47,181
Cut!
No!

155
00:05:47,222 --> 00:05:50,851
Or cut, you know,
that's your call.

156
00:05:53,728 --> 00:05:55,022
Everything was delicious.

157
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:56,606
Thank you.
It was.

158
00:05:56,648 --> 00:05:58,317
The duck in particular
was superb.

159
00:05:58,357 --> 00:05:59,526
Thank you.

160
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:05,991
You haven't said anything.

161
00:06:06,033 --> 00:06:08,160
Actually, I do have
one small complaint.

162
00:06:08,202 --> 00:06:13,498
Oh. Well, please, I...
I welcome criticism.

163
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,084
Your musician--
right outside the restaurant--

164
00:06:16,126 --> 00:06:17,460
is kind of a mood-killer.

165
00:06:17,502 --> 00:06:19,046
What musician?

166
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:21,840
♪ And there's a country
called Argentina ♪

167
00:06:21,882 --> 00:06:24,843
♪ It's a place I've never seen ♪

168
00:06:24,885 --> 00:06:28,347
♪ But I'm told for 50 pesos ♪

169
00:06:28,387 --> 00:06:31,308
♪ You can buy a human spleen ♪

170
00:06:31,350 --> 00:06:35,354
♪ Human spleen... ♪

171
00:06:35,394 --> 00:06:36,646
♪ Olé! ♪

172
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:40,234
What are you doing here?

173
00:06:40,275 --> 00:06:42,694
Well, you said you had customers
lined up in the streets,

174
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:43,862
so I'm here to entertain.

175
00:06:43,904 --> 00:06:45,530
Oh, great.
Yeah!

176
00:06:45,572 --> 00:06:47,324
It really has
been great, too.

177
00:06:47,366 --> 00:06:49,910
You know, some of these people
must have seen me play before,

178
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:52,037
because they were requesting
a bunch of my songs.

179
00:06:52,079 --> 00:06:56,791
Yeah, "You Suck" and, um...
"Shut Up and Go Home."

180
00:06:56,833 --> 00:07:00,087
Um, listen, Phoebe...
Yeah?

181
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:02,964
You know how much I love
listening to your music.

182
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:04,507
You know, but...

183
00:07:04,549 --> 00:07:06,343
But what?

184
00:07:06,385 --> 00:07:10,180
Um, well, this is kind
of a classy place.

185
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:13,058
Okay, say no more.

186
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:15,810
♪ It wasn't just
that she was fat ♪

187
00:07:15,852 --> 00:07:17,312
♪ The woman smelled
like garbage ♪

188
00:07:17,354 --> 00:07:18,772
Everyone!

189
00:07:18,813 --> 00:07:20,107
♪ It wasn't just
that she was fat ♪

190
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:23,651
♪ The woman smelled
like garbage. ♪

191
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:25,612
Classy, huh?

192
00:07:31,450 --> 00:07:32,411
Hi. Chandler Bing.

193
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:33,620
I have a reservation.

194
00:07:33,661 --> 00:07:34,996
Welcome to
the Chestnut Inn, Mr. Bing.

195
00:07:35,038 --> 00:07:36,206
So where are you
joining us from?

196
00:07:36,248 --> 00:07:37,249
New York.

197
00:07:37,291 --> 00:07:39,167
The Big Apple!

198
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:40,168
I'm sorry.

199
00:07:40,210 --> 00:07:41,795
He's a little bit wound up.

200
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:43,713
We had to stop at every maple
candy stand on the way here.

201
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:46,216
I ate all my gifts
for everybody!

202
00:07:48,385 --> 00:07:50,095
I'm sorry, Mr. Bing,
there's no record

203
00:07:50,137 --> 00:07:51,805
of your reservation
in the computer.

204
00:07:51,846 --> 00:07:52,847
Well, that's impossible.

205
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:54,599
Can you check again,
please?

206
00:07:54,641 --> 00:07:56,101
( falsetto ):
Can you check
again, please?

207
00:07:57,602 --> 00:07:58,937
I'm sorry. It's not here.

208
00:07:58,979 --> 00:08:00,688
It's not there.

209
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:02,190
Let me get this straight.

210
00:08:02,232 --> 00:08:04,901
I called yesterday
to try to cancel
my reservation

211
00:08:04,943 --> 00:08:06,778
and was told
it's not refundable.

212
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,529
Then we drove six hours
all the way up here,

213
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:11,325
and now you're telling me that
we don't have a reservation?

214
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:12,451
I don't know what to say.

215
00:08:12,491 --> 00:08:14,786
She doesn't know
what to say.

216
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:17,164
Just give us
the cheapest room you have.

217
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:18,623
Well, unfortunately,
the only thing

218
00:08:18,665 --> 00:08:20,250
we have available
is our deluxe suite.

219
00:08:20,292 --> 00:08:21,376
The rate is $600.

220
00:08:21,418 --> 00:08:22,543
That's insane!

221
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:24,045
That is totally insane.

222
00:08:24,087 --> 00:08:25,880
Dude, let's drive home.

223
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:28,883
We'll hit all the
maple candy stores
on the way back,

224
00:08:28,925 --> 00:08:30,260
and if they're closed,

225
00:08:30,302 --> 00:08:33,054
maybe we'll tap a tree
and make some ourselves.

226
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:38,977
Does that room have a closet
I can lock him in?

227
00:08:39,019 --> 00:08:40,479
We'll take it.

228
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,397
Great.

229
00:08:42,439 --> 00:08:44,649
They are totally
ripping us off!

230
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:45,942
Dude, don't worry about it.

231
00:08:45,984 --> 00:08:47,568
I know how we can make
your money back.

232
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:48,903
This is a nice hotel, you know.

233
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:50,155
Plenty of amenities.

234
00:08:50,197 --> 00:08:51,739
We just load up on those.

235
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:53,158
Like those apples.

236
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:57,578
Instead of taking one,
um... I take six.

237
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:00,999
Great. At $100 an apple,
we're there.

238
00:09:01,041 --> 00:09:03,001
Come on, you get the idea.

239
00:09:03,043 --> 00:09:05,962
You know, we'll make our
money back in no time.

240
00:09:06,004 --> 00:09:07,297
Dude, you're shaking.

241
00:09:07,339 --> 00:09:08,423
I think it's the sugar.

242
00:09:08,465 --> 00:09:09,632
Can you hold the apple?

243
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:16,681
Hi.

244
00:09:16,723 --> 00:09:18,141
Hey.

245
00:09:18,183 --> 00:09:19,851
Joey, I got to tell you:

246
00:09:19,893 --> 00:09:21,520
I have been thinking all day
about that scene you did.

247
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:24,439
I mean, you
were amazing.

248
00:09:24,481 --> 00:09:26,649
Oh, you know,
the writing was good,

249
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:28,276
you know,
and the director's good,

250
00:09:28,318 --> 00:09:30,445
and-and my co-star's good,

251
00:09:30,487 --> 00:09:32,489
but they're not as good as me!

252
00:09:32,531 --> 00:09:36,117
Come on, you have to tell me
what happens tomorrow.

253
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:37,577
Oh, just going over
the script now.

254
00:09:37,618 --> 00:09:38,995
Do you want to read lines
with me?

255
00:09:39,037 --> 00:09:42,749
Me? Oh, I... I'm not an actress.

256
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:44,000
Oh, well, I can ask Monica.

257
00:09:44,042 --> 00:09:45,460
Screw her! That part is mine.

258
00:09:45,502 --> 00:09:47,087
Right.

259
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:49,630
Okay, so, uh, so just from
the top of the page, right here.

260
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:50,798
Okay.

261
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,551
( inhales deeply )

262
00:09:54,553 --> 00:09:55,970
"Hello, Drake.

263
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:57,972
I'm surprised
to see you here."

264
00:09:58,014 --> 00:09:59,598
"I can't believe
you married him."

265
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:01,393
"Well, what choice
did I have?

266
00:10:01,435 --> 00:10:04,062
He was keeping my
sister in a dungeon."

267
00:10:07,357 --> 00:10:08,483
So what about us?

268
00:10:08,525 --> 00:10:10,777
Everything we feel
for each other?"

269
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:12,028
"It's over.

270
00:10:12,070 --> 00:10:13,613
You have to accept that."

271
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:14,989
"How can I?

272
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:18,034
"Knowing I'll never hold you
in my arms again?

273
00:10:18,076 --> 00:10:22,330
"Or touch your skin
or feel your lips?

274
00:10:22,372 --> 00:10:25,666
"Knowing I'll never
make love to you?

275
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:28,044
How can I accept that"

276
00:10:28,086 --> 00:10:29,588
"I can never kiss you again

277
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:32,382
when it's all I can do
not to kiss you right now?"

278
00:10:35,552 --> 00:10:36,886
Kiss me.

279
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:39,847
What?

280
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:42,016
Kiss me.

281
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:44,185
Uh, Rach, it doesn't say that.

282
00:10:44,227 --> 00:10:47,314
No, I'm saying it.

283
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:48,398
But... but...

284
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:50,733
Just... don't talk.

285
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:53,528
( gasping ):
Oh!

286
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:59,659
Well, that's new.

287
00:11:08,335 --> 00:11:10,587
Hi.

288
00:11:10,629 --> 00:11:12,172
This is Ross Geller
in suite 206.

289
00:11:12,213 --> 00:11:14,257
Um, I seem to have forgotten
a couple of things.

290
00:11:14,299 --> 00:11:16,468
Could-could you have some
complimentary toiletries

291
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:17,636
sent up to my room?

292
00:11:17,676 --> 00:11:19,638
Thank you.

293
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:22,140
Okay, um, toothbrush,
toothpaste,

294
00:11:22,182 --> 00:11:24,142
razor, mouthwash, deodorant,

295
00:11:24,184 --> 00:11:26,144
dental floss, Band-Aids,

296
00:11:26,186 --> 00:11:28,647
shaving cream, aftershave...

297
00:11:28,687 --> 00:11:30,524
and I feel
like I'm forgetting something.

298
00:11:30,565 --> 00:11:32,192
Um, is there anything else
you have

299
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:35,654
that I haven't asked for
already?

300
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:36,821
Yeah. Go ahead.

301
00:11:36,863 --> 00:11:39,324
Send up some tampons.

302
00:11:39,366 --> 00:11:40,492
Thank you.

303
00:11:40,534 --> 00:11:41,700
( catching his breath )

304
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:42,827
What did you get?

305
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:43,995
USA Today.

306
00:11:44,037 --> 00:11:45,580
Nice. Put it
with the others.

307
00:11:45,622 --> 00:11:47,582
And I also got...

308
00:11:47,624 --> 00:11:49,750
two more apples.

309
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:51,836
We're four short of a bushel.

310
00:11:51,878 --> 00:11:53,880
God, I feel so alive!

311
00:11:53,921 --> 00:11:56,550
I love being
in the country.

312
00:11:56,591 --> 00:11:57,800
I also got

313
00:11:57,842 --> 00:11:59,344
these great
salt and pepper shakers

314
00:11:59,386 --> 00:12:00,345
from the restaurant.

315
00:12:00,387 --> 00:12:01,804
Ooh, that's not cool.

316
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:05,724
Dude, none of this is cool.

317
00:12:05,766 --> 00:12:08,520
Look, Chandler,
you have to find the line

318
00:12:08,562 --> 00:12:12,440
between stealing and-and taking
what the hotel owes you.

319
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:15,402
Um, for example,
a hair dryer-- no, no, no.

320
00:12:15,443 --> 00:12:17,153
But shampoos and
conditioners--

321
00:12:17,195 --> 00:12:18,697
oh, yes, yes, yes.

322
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:22,033
Now, the-the
salt shaker

323
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:23,326
is off-limits. Uh!

324
00:12:23,368 --> 00:12:26,871
But the salt...

325
00:12:26,913 --> 00:12:29,541
I wish I'd thought this through.

326
00:12:29,583 --> 00:12:31,876
I think I get
what you mean, though.

327
00:12:31,918 --> 00:12:33,920
Like, the lamp is, uh,

328
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:36,172
is the hotel's,
but the bulbs...

329
00:12:36,214 --> 00:12:37,965
Oh, you already got that?

330
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:40,801
Not my first time
in a hotel, my friend.

331
00:12:40,843 --> 00:12:42,011
Okay, uh,

332
00:12:42,053 --> 00:12:43,012
how about this?

333
00:12:43,054 --> 00:12:44,138
No, no, no.

334
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:46,224
You can't
take the remote control.

335
00:12:46,266 --> 00:12:48,727
Yes, but the batteries.

336
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:54,190
Thank you.

337
00:12:54,232 --> 00:12:55,734
Thank you very much.

338
00:12:55,774 --> 00:12:57,736
Ooh, ooh. Let's-let's celebrate
with some maple candy.

339
00:12:57,776 --> 00:12:59,070
No!

340
00:13:00,405 --> 00:13:02,407
At least tell me
where you hid it.

341
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,705
Can I ask you a question?

342
00:13:08,747 --> 00:13:10,373
Yeah.

343
00:13:10,415 --> 00:13:14,085
Have you ever had any...

344
00:13:14,127 --> 00:13:19,215
weird... romantic... dreams?

345
00:13:19,257 --> 00:13:21,259
Hmm. Let me think.

346
00:13:21,301 --> 00:13:22,594
Oh.

347
00:13:22,636 --> 00:13:24,429
When I was younger,
I used to dream

348
00:13:24,471 --> 00:13:26,889
that I got married
to Mayor McCheese.

349
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:29,976
And-and on our wedding
night, I ate his head.

350
00:13:31,436 --> 00:13:33,812
Okay.

351
00:13:33,854 --> 00:13:36,232
Well, this is like that...

352
00:13:36,274 --> 00:13:38,234
in no way.

353
00:13:38,276 --> 00:13:39,736
I had a...

354
00:13:39,778 --> 00:13:42,405
I had a dream last night
that I wanted to kiss Joey.

355
00:13:42,447 --> 00:13:43,864
Wow.

356
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:45,824
You mean, like, like,
"kiss him" kiss him?

357
00:13:45,866 --> 00:13:47,076
Oh, yeah.

358
00:13:47,118 --> 00:13:48,411
I mean,
it was pretty intense.

359
00:13:48,453 --> 00:13:49,704
Wow.

360
00:13:49,746 --> 00:13:50,747
What do you think
brought that on?

361
00:13:50,789 --> 00:13:52,039
I don't know.

362
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:53,374
Maybe it has something
to do with the fact

363
00:13:53,416 --> 00:13:54,959
that I saw him
do a love scene yesterday.

364
00:13:55,001 --> 00:13:56,670
A love scene?
With-with who?

365
00:13:56,711 --> 00:13:57,462
Olivia.

366
00:13:57,504 --> 00:13:58,755
Olivia?!

367
00:13:58,797 --> 00:14:00,089
I thought she was
marrying Connor?

368
00:14:00,131 --> 00:14:01,758
Oh.
Oh, right.

369
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:04,260
Real life more important.

370
00:14:04,302 --> 00:14:06,680
So, do you think
that my dream means anything?

371
00:14:06,721 --> 00:14:08,014
I don't know.

372
00:14:08,055 --> 00:14:09,932
I mean, you saw him
do a love scene.

373
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:12,435
So, maybe you don't
have a thing for Joey.

374
00:14:12,477 --> 00:14:14,354
Maybe you have
a thing for Drake.

375
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:16,690
Huh.

376
00:14:18,024 --> 00:14:20,485
Well, it was Joey
reading Drake's lines

377
00:14:20,527 --> 00:14:22,529
in the dream.

378
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:23,822
Of course it was.

379
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:24,989
Trust me.

380
00:14:25,031 --> 00:14:26,700
When it comes
to psychology,

381
00:14:26,741 --> 00:14:28,576
I know what I'm
talking about.

382
00:14:28,618 --> 00:14:30,829
I took two psych
classes in college.

383
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:32,246
Oh.

384
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:34,248
You took the same class twice.

385
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:35,375
It was hard.

386
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:37,001
I...

387
00:14:37,043 --> 00:14:38,127
Hey.

388
00:14:38,169 --> 00:14:39,295
Hi.

389
00:14:39,337 --> 00:14:40,839
Hey.

390
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:41,964
Here, Monica.
Look what I
got to wear

391
00:14:42,006 --> 00:14:43,341
when I play at
your restaurant.

392
00:14:43,383 --> 00:14:45,426
Ha!

393
00:14:47,679 --> 00:14:49,263
Uh, uh.

394
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:51,725
Wait.

395
00:14:51,766 --> 00:14:54,185
Right?

396
00:14:54,227 --> 00:14:55,936
I think this might even class up

397
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:58,022
"The Ballad
of the Uncircumcised Man."

398
00:14:59,065 --> 00:15:01,192
Um... Phoebe?

399
00:15:01,234 --> 00:15:02,485
Hmm?

400
00:15:02,527 --> 00:15:04,487
Maybe I wasn't clear before.

401
00:15:04,529 --> 00:15:08,199
But I really love
listening to your music here,

402
00:15:08,241 --> 00:15:12,370
but my restaurant--
it's sort of an upscale place.

403
00:15:12,412 --> 00:15:14,163
Right, yeah, okay.

404
00:15:14,205 --> 00:15:18,292
I'll ask the butler to fetch
my diamonds out of the vault.

405
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:20,461
Phoebe, it's not
what you wear...

406
00:15:20,503 --> 00:15:23,673
it's sort of your songs.

407
00:15:23,715 --> 00:15:26,925
I just don't think you should
play at the restaurant anymore.

408
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:29,637
Oh.

409
00:15:29,679 --> 00:15:31,097
Okay.

410
00:15:31,138 --> 00:15:33,433
Fine, I'll just... I'll...

411
00:15:33,474 --> 00:15:35,017
I'll take the hat back.

412
00:15:36,853 --> 00:15:38,897
There.

413
00:15:44,277 --> 00:15:45,820
Hey.

414
00:15:45,862 --> 00:15:47,988
So, you guys, the funniest thing
happened at work...

415
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:50,283
What, my songs aren't good
enough for your restaurant?

416
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:53,077
Okay, we're still on that.

417
00:15:53,119 --> 00:15:55,538
I didn't say your songs
weren't good enough.

418
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:56,955
Well, then what's wrong
with them?

419
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:58,332
What, they don't go with

420
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:00,084
your tiny portions
of pretentious food?

421
00:16:00,126 --> 00:16:02,545
Tiny portions?

422
00:16:02,587 --> 00:16:03,963
Yeah, well, um, "Excuse me,

423
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:05,757
"I ordered the smoked
salmon appetizer.

424
00:16:05,799 --> 00:16:08,927
But I can't see it.
I can't see it."

425
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:13,180
Phoebe, it's not about quantity.

426
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:15,057
Well, it's not about quality.

427
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:16,601
Oh... oh, really?

428
00:16:16,643 --> 00:16:18,311
You want to talk
about quality?

429
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:19,938
Have you ever heard of "a key"?

430
00:16:19,978 --> 00:16:22,816
It's what some people sing in.

431
00:16:22,857 --> 00:16:25,984
Well, at least all my songs
don't taste like garlic.

432
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:29,697
Yeah, there are
other ingredients, Monica.

433
00:16:29,739 --> 00:16:31,741
Oh, okay, so that's
what we're doing.

434
00:16:31,783 --> 00:16:33,785
Well, you know what,
when I'm in the coffeehouse

435
00:16:33,827 --> 00:16:35,536
bopping along
to one of your songs,

436
00:16:35,578 --> 00:16:37,037
I'm wearing ear plugs.

437
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:39,373
Ear plugs? Or cloves of garlic?

438
00:16:39,415 --> 00:16:42,126
You know what?
You know what?

439
00:16:42,168 --> 00:16:43,503
I take back
what I said before.

440
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:45,129
You keep playing
at the restaurant.

441
00:16:45,171 --> 00:16:47,298
Because with your music
driving people inside,

442
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:49,467
my bar sales
have gone up like crazy.

443
00:16:49,509 --> 00:16:52,637
What are people having,
the garlic martini?!

444
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:56,474
Here's your copy
of the bill.

445
00:16:56,516 --> 00:16:57,892
We hope you
enjoyed your stay.

446
00:16:57,934 --> 00:16:59,017
Oh, we did.

447
00:16:59,059 --> 00:17:00,728
And you still have
all your lamps.

448
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:05,859
Well, I didn't
factor in the room tax.

449
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:07,610
Oh, dude, don't
worry about it.

450
00:17:07,652 --> 00:17:09,570
I found an unattended
maid's cart.

451
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:11,197
We're way ahead
of the game.

452
00:17:12,907 --> 00:17:13,950
Oh, my God.

453
00:17:13,992 --> 00:17:15,326
What?

454
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:18,078
There's something new
in the bowl.

455
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,164
Look, we have enough.
Just walk away.

456
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:23,167
But I-I want...
I want the pine cones.

457
00:17:23,209 --> 00:17:26,504
There's a forest
right outside.

458
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:27,755
It's not the same.

459
00:17:27,797 --> 00:17:29,256
Okay, go quick.

460
00:17:32,385 --> 00:17:34,178
( caws )

461
00:17:37,015 --> 00:17:40,226
Thank you for
a delightful stay.

462
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:49,986
Oh, my maple candy!

463
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:57,035
♪ The food here at Javu ♪

464
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:58,369
♪ Will kill you ♪

465
00:17:58,411 --> 00:18:00,830
♪ The food here at Javu ♪

466
00:18:00,872 --> 00:18:02,081
♪ Will kill you ♪

467
00:18:02,122 --> 00:18:03,875
Oh, thank God
it's just you.

468
00:18:03,917 --> 00:18:07,211
I thought someone
was swinging a bag of cats
against the wall.

469
00:18:07,253 --> 00:18:09,129
You better get back
in that kitchen, Monica.

470
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:11,173
The garlic's not going
to overuse itself.

471
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:14,343
Okay, you have
to stop playing now.

472
00:18:14,385 --> 00:18:17,221
Why? The only person my playing
is bothering is you.

473
00:18:17,263 --> 00:18:18,305
Oh, yeah?

474
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:19,682
Okay, let's settle this.
Come on.

475
00:18:19,724 --> 00:18:22,643
Get your garlic peelers off me.

476
00:18:22,685 --> 00:18:24,938
Excuse me. Excuse me.

477
00:18:24,979 --> 00:18:28,983
Hi, I'm Monica Gellar.
I'm the head chef here.

478
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:31,360
Okay, I was actually
expecting a little
applause there,

479
00:18:31,402 --> 00:18:33,111
but whatever. Okay.

480
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:35,949
Okay, quick question:
By a show of hands,

481
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:39,326
how many of you were bothered
by this woman's singing outside?

482
00:18:40,787 --> 00:18:42,162
Okay, okay.

483
00:18:42,204 --> 00:18:44,999
How many of you enjoyed
the music outside?

484
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:47,334
Ha.

485
00:18:47,376 --> 00:18:48,502
All right.

486
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:49,963
Let me ask you
this question.

487
00:18:50,004 --> 00:18:51,631
How many of you thought
the music was fine

488
00:18:51,672 --> 00:18:53,466
but not in keeping with
the tone of the restaurant?

489
00:18:53,507 --> 00:18:55,051
Okay, well...

490
00:18:55,093 --> 00:18:57,303
who identified the tone
of this restaurant

491
00:18:57,344 --> 00:19:00,473
as pretentious comma garlicky?

492
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:02,934
Okay. Who thinks
the food is delicious

493
00:19:02,976 --> 00:19:05,686
and a little pretension
never hurt anyone?

494
00:19:07,354 --> 00:19:08,731
Okay, well, all right.

495
00:19:08,773 --> 00:19:11,025
Who thinks the food is fine,
the music was fine,

496
00:19:11,067 --> 00:19:14,695
but your evening was ruined
by this incessant poll taking?

497
00:19:18,032 --> 00:19:19,659
Excuse us.

498
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:25,539
All right,
here's a question.

499
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:29,669
Who was so worried about
her restaurant being fancy

500
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:33,047
that she made a big deal about
her friend playing her music

501
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:36,592
and feels really bad
about it now?

502
00:19:36,634 --> 00:19:37,760
Oh.

503
00:19:37,802 --> 00:19:40,429
Well, who was so stupid
and stubborn

504
00:19:40,471 --> 00:19:42,723
that she lashed out
against her friend's cooking

505
00:19:42,765 --> 00:19:46,310
which she actually thinks
is pretty great?

506
00:19:46,352 --> 00:19:48,354
I'm sorry.
I'm sorry, too.

507
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:51,107
Hey, you want
to stick around

508
00:19:51,149 --> 00:19:52,692
and I'll whip you up
some dinner?

509
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:54,735
Yeah, as long as it's free.

510
00:19:54,777 --> 00:19:57,613
Food here is
ridiculously overpr...

511
00:20:00,033 --> 00:20:02,368
Who's hoping the hand-raising
thing is still cute enough

512
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:03,953
that you won't hate me?

513
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,458
Hey.
Hey.

514
00:20:10,835 --> 00:20:12,461
Joey...

515
00:20:12,503 --> 00:20:14,296
do you have peanut butter
on the back of your head?

516
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:22,055
Oh, man, I thought
I got it all.

517
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:24,223
How...?

518
00:20:24,264 --> 00:20:26,017
How?

519
00:20:26,059 --> 00:20:28,686
Well, I was making
a peanut butter smoothie, right.

520
00:20:28,728 --> 00:20:30,771
And I couldn't find the...

521
00:20:30,813 --> 00:20:33,607
this little plastic
thingy that goes in
the top of the blender.

522
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:37,195
And I thought, well, you know,
"How important can be, right?"

523
00:20:37,235 --> 00:20:39,739
It turns out, very.

524
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:41,991
Wow.

525
00:20:42,033 --> 00:20:43,450
Definitely just Drake.

526
00:20:43,492 --> 00:20:44,994
What?

527
00:20:45,036 --> 00:20:46,328
How's it going with Drake?

528
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:47,663
Oh.

529
00:20:47,705 --> 00:20:48,706
I don't think
it's going very well.

530
00:20:48,748 --> 00:20:49,790
What?

531
00:20:49,832 --> 00:20:51,834
That scene I saw was so good.

532
00:20:51,876 --> 00:20:56,672
Well, I'm feeling really
insecure about the one
we're shooting tomorrow.

533
00:20:56,714 --> 00:20:59,508
Joey, is this that thing that
you do when you say you're bad,

534
00:20:59,550 --> 00:21:01,094
so I'll give you a compliment?

535
00:21:01,135 --> 00:21:02,261
A little.

536
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:05,848
No, but I really
am worried.

537
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:08,059
I mean, I have
to make it convincing that...

538
00:21:08,101 --> 00:21:09,727
that I'm in love with Olivia.

539
00:21:09,769 --> 00:21:10,978
So?

540
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:13,064
So, I've never played that.

541
00:21:13,106 --> 00:21:15,108
Oh, honey,
it can't be that hard.

542
00:21:15,149 --> 00:21:17,110
I mean, you've been
in love before.

543
00:21:17,151 --> 00:21:20,696
Uh, well... just once.

544
00:21:20,738 --> 00:21:23,616
With you.

545
00:21:23,657 --> 00:21:25,785
Okay.

546
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:27,285
This could be a little awkward.

547
00:21:27,327 --> 00:21:28,913
I'm just going to blow past it.

548
00:21:28,955 --> 00:21:33,209
Well, can't you just use
that method, that actor thing

549
00:21:33,251 --> 00:21:35,044
where you use
your real-life memories

550
00:21:35,086 --> 00:21:36,963
to help you in your performance?

551
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:40,800
What the hell are you
talking about?

552
00:21:43,469 --> 00:21:45,638
All right.
All right, look, just, um...

553
00:21:45,679 --> 00:21:48,766
just try to remember how
you felt when you were in love

554
00:21:48,808 --> 00:21:51,602
and think about that
when you're playing the scene.

555
00:21:51,644 --> 00:21:52,812
Oh.

556
00:21:55,064 --> 00:21:56,274
Okay.

557
00:21:56,314 --> 00:21:57,316
Yeah.

558
00:21:57,357 --> 00:21:58,484
I think I can do that.

559
00:21:58,525 --> 00:21:59,610
Yeah, okay.

560
00:21:59,652 --> 00:22:01,487
There's this party scene
coming up

561
00:22:01,528 --> 00:22:04,031
and Olivia and
her husband are there

562
00:22:04,073 --> 00:22:06,284
and all Drake wants to do
is grab her and kiss her,

563
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:09,620
but he can't.

564
00:22:09,662 --> 00:22:12,123
And that makes me think about
all those times

565
00:22:12,165 --> 00:22:14,834
I wanted to grab you and
kiss you, but you didn't know,

566
00:22:14,875 --> 00:22:17,377
so I would just pretend
everything was cool,

567
00:22:17,419 --> 00:22:19,797
but really it was killing me.

568
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:23,550
Joey, you never...

569
00:22:23,592 --> 00:22:25,803
you never talked about
that before.

570
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:30,808
Hey, you know what else
I could use?

571
00:22:30,850 --> 00:22:34,312
There's this scene where Drake
sneaks into Olivia's bedroom

572
00:22:34,352 --> 00:22:35,896
and she doesn't know
he's there--

573
00:22:35,938 --> 00:22:37,773
which never happened with us.

574
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:42,611
He knows he shouldn't
be there,

575
00:22:42,653 --> 00:22:48,242
but he just wants
to look at her, you know.

576
00:22:48,284 --> 00:22:50,368
And I remember
all those mornings

577
00:22:50,410 --> 00:22:52,496
before you even
put on your makeup

578
00:22:52,538 --> 00:22:58,919
when I would think to myself,
"My God, she is beautiful."

579
00:22:58,961 --> 00:23:02,798
And it hurt so much
because I knew

580
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:08,095
I could never tell you.

581
00:23:08,137 --> 00:23:12,933
But it was worth it just
to be there looking at you.

582
00:23:18,981 --> 00:23:20,900
Thanks, dude.
This is great!

583
00:23:23,152 --> 00:23:24,402
( door closes )

584
00:23:33,329 --> 00:23:35,664
Besides tampons and salt?

585
00:23:37,250 --> 00:23:38,959
Oh. Oh, my God.

586
00:23:39,001 --> 00:23:40,378
Maple candy.

587
00:23:40,418 --> 00:23:41,962
That's so sweet of you.

588
00:23:42,004 --> 00:23:43,589
Mmm...

589
00:23:43,630 --> 00:23:45,758
That's weird; it's empty.

590
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:46,884
Hi, you guys.

591
00:23:46,926 --> 00:23:48,052
What's going on?

592
00:23:48,094 --> 00:23:51,429
You-you guys want
to hang out or...?

593
00:23:57,644 --> 00:23:59,646
Do you, do you guys
hear a buzzing?

594
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:02,482
